(6217854, 916881, 122131, '<td valign="top">It''s unfortunate that the photo is so blurry -- I love the motion going up the escalator, and the people going about their morning, but if you had mounted the camera on a sturdy tripod and made the escalator, the rails, walls and roof static, whilst capturing motion all around it, it would have been a more powerful shot.<br/>5 from me.</td>', 'It''s unfortunate that the photo is so blurry -- I love the motion going up the escalator, and the people going about their morning, but if you had mounted the camera on a sturdy tripod and made the escalator, the rails, walls and roof static, whilst capturing motion all around it, it would have been a more powerful shot.5 from me.', '2010-11-09 18:01:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6217856, 917070, 122131, '<td valign="top">I''m sure a lot of people will mark this down because, whilst it might have been taken at 4:35am, it wouldn''t have made a difference than if it were taken at 2 in the afternoon.. <br/>In any case, I love the symmetry. It''s eye-catching and has a certain ''wow'' factor to it. I certainly hope it''s a shot you had "prepared earlier"!<br/>The background does seem a bit noisy, particularly toward the bottom.<br/>7 from me.</td>', 'I''m sure a lot of people will mark this down because, whilst it might have been taken at 4:35am, it wouldn''t have made a difference than if it were taken at 2 in the afternoon.. In any case, I love the symmetry. It''s eye-catching and has a certain ''wow'' factor to it. I certainly hope it''s a shot you had "prepared earlier"!The background does seem a bit noisy, particularly toward the bottom.7 from me.', '2010-11-09 18:04:35.000000', NULL, 1),
