(6218244, 917729, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> congratulations, Robert! The first place could get away with a 4s exposure at 800ISO, and you needed 66s at 1600. Rural life is harder :). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was about to comment on that, over there :-) Not only that, he was stopped down a stop and a half more. It really has me scratching my head, mainly over how he managed a blue sky... I mean, if the sky''s lit by ambient reflected light, wouldn''t be a much warmer color? CF my clouds... It''s all a mystery to me :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: congratulations, Robert! The first place could get away with a 4s exposure at 800ISO, and you needed 66s at 1600. Rural life is harder :).   I was about to comment on that, over there :-) Not only that, he was stopped down a stop and a half more. It really has me scratching my head, mainly over how he managed a blue sky... I mean, if the sky''s lit by ambient reflected light, wouldn''t be a much warmer color? CF my clouds... It''s all a mystery to me :-)', '2010-11-10 00:37:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6218281, 917729, 121949, '<td valign="top">congrats, this is a great photo. I had you pegged as one of the winners!</td>', 'congrats, this is a great photo. I had you pegged as one of the winners!', '2010-11-10 00:57:33.000000', NULL, 0),
